# warehouse

The warehouse gateway is a codefly/warehouse/v0 gRPC service in front of a SQL
warehouse. A generated service declares `backend: mem`, the catalog-only backend
that needs no warehouse credentials. Set `backend` in service.codefly.yaml to
choose another engine; removing it falls back to the unsupported DuckDB skeleton.
See https://github.com/codefly-dev/service-warehouse for current backend support.

A local run starts the gateway image with a fresh shared secret and hands it to
consumers as the secret `token` value of the `warehouse` configuration group.
Both Start and Test wait for health and authenticated Capabilities.

Deployment requires an environment-managed Kubernetes secret reference for
SWH_AUTH_TOKEN. Bind the same secret key to each consumer's warehouse.token
configuration. The agent renders a same-namespace ingress NetworkPolicy and a
dedicated ServiceAccount; a policy-capable CNI is required. See the repository
README for both secret bindings and workload-identity setup.
